// Win32 platform layer for ugui apps (see NOSDL.md for the platform API)
// - wWinMain() converts command line to UTF-8 argv and calls app's appMain()
// - all events are generated by WindowProc (or pushed by app via SDL_PushEvent) into eventQueue, then
//   dispatched by platformProcessEvents(); event handlers are never called from inside WindowProc, so
//   platformProcessEvents() can be called from an event handler (nested event loop)
// - input: WM_POINTER (Win 8+) for mouse, touch, and pen (w/ GetPointerPenInfoHistory for all pen points);
//   plain WM_MOUSE* fallback if WM_POINTER not available
// - rendering: WGL (OpenGL 3.3 core) or software (app draws to platformGetSWFramebuffer(), we blit w/ GDI)
// - app must load GL functions itself (e.g. gladLoadGL()) after platformInit() if USE_GL is still set
// - no app-specific code here
// refs:
// - https://github.com/blender/blender/blob/main/intern/ghost/intern/GHOST_SystemWin32.cc
// - https://github.com/glfw/glfw/blob/master/src/wgl_context.c

#ifndef WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
#define WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
#endif
